 "capsule": "Unlike its Ascanian-era Margraviate phase, this 1422–1619 Electorate of Brandenburg was the Hohenzollern electoral state founded by Frederick I (invested 1417): his descendant Joachim II brought it to Lutheranism in 1539, and Johann Sigismund's 1618 inheritance of the Duchy of Prussia, secured shortly before his death in 1619, set up the future Brandenburg-Prussia.",
